
Linux on the ESP32-S31-Function-CoreBoard-1: RV32 at 320 MHz, 16 MiB PSRAM.

Ethernet  eth0 gets an address with DHCP at boot: ip addr show eth0
Wi-Fi     wpa_passphrase "<ssid>" "<passphrase>" >> /etc/wpa_supplicant.conf
          /etc/init.d/S40wifi restart (/mnt/usb/wpa_supplicant.conf wins)
          iw dev wlan0 link; /usr/share/examples/wifi-scan.sh
Bluetooth bluetoothctl, then: scan le, scan bredr, devices
          Home Assistant: /usr/share/examples/ha-bluetooth.sh HA_ADDRESS
Thread    thread-start, then ot-ctl state; thread-start stop ends it
          thread-share: a key for a phone app
          Home Assistant: /usr/share/examples/ha-thread.sh HA_ADDRESS
VPN       WireGuard: /usr/share/examples/wg-setup.sh, /etc/default/wireguard
MQTT      mosquitto_pub, mosquitto_sub; /etc/default/mqtt, mqtt-report.sh
Firewall  nft list ruleset; open a port until the next boot:
          nft insert rule inet filter input tcp dport 8080 accept
System    htop, free, df -h, ncdu, dmesg, tmux
Network   ssh, scp, curl, links, iperf3, tcpdump
Files     nnn, tree; /mnt/usb is the FAT partition of the USB stick
Code      micropython, lua, vim, nano, sqlite3, bc, gdbserver, strace
GPIO      pinctrl, gpioinfo, gpioget, gpioset, gpiomon (edges)
          /usr/share/examples/gpio-watch.sh PIN, button.sh PIN COMMAND
Examples  ls /usr/share/examples
